# Every changelog entry is added at the top of the same "## [Unreleased]" section, so
# any two PRs open at once conflict on that one line however unrelated their code is.
# The resolution is always "keep both bullets", which is exactly what a union merge does.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# Guarded by src/lib/__tests__/changelogShape.test.ts, which runs in the pre-commit hook
# — because the note below asked people to check and that was not enough, twice.
#
# Union keeps both sides of a hunk without
# understanding structure, so when two branches each CREATE the "## [Unreleased]" header
# — rather than adding to an existing one — it keeps both, and the changelog ends up with
# two Unreleased sections. That happened between 0.24.0 and 0.24.1 and would have shipped
# a release missing half its entries, since the release workflow reads only the first
# matching section. Merging the duplicates by hand takes a moment; noticing at release
# time does not happen by itself.
